--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Wednesday, the 7th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in an evening paper that almost every day is inaugural day somewhere in the United States, during the first weeks of the New Year, as governors in thirty-three states take the oath of office, and the advent of new administrations in many states recalls Democratic victories of the election in November.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Wednesday, the 7th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I was glad to learn that almost every day is inaugural day somewhere in the United States during the first weeks of the New Year as governors in 33 states take the oath of office as designated by their constitutions. The advent of new administrations in many states recalls the Democratic victories of the election in America, which I hope may be followed by prosperity there.

