--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Thursday, the 8th of January, 1931 (2/3 key facts kept) ---
I read in the evening paper that Britons were astonished at reports of widely extended insubordination at the naval yard at Devonport, and France mourned her “savior,” Marshal Joffre, as his funeral passed through the streets of Paris. Mrs. Dot Mahoney asked me for the loan of two shillings, which I refused.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Thursday, the 8th of January, 1931 (0/5 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald: Paris mourned Marshal Joffre.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Thursday, the 8th of January, 1931 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
To-day the auditors come on Monday.
